edia.org/wiki/Terri_Schiavo"/></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>Ohio Hospice and Palliative Care Organization</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.ohpco.org/"/><comment>Click on Consumers, Living Will.</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="other"><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.uslivingwillregistry.com/forms.shtm"/></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bernal</surname><given-names>EW</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Ford P, Duzinski D</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Listening to the Husband</article-title><source>Complex Ethics Consultations: Cases that Haunt Us</source><publisher-name>Cambridge: Cambridge University Press</publisher-name><comment></comment></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>